## The Numbers Speak Loudest

To kick things off, 2026 has already seen a staggering 144 Class I recalls--those are the 'serious risk to health' kind. Compare that to just 35 Class III recalls, and it's clear: brands are playing with fire and getting burned.

## Who's on the Naughty List?

The data showcases some consistent offenders. Moonlight Packing Corporation and Ghirardelli Chocolate Company top the list with failing grades, each with double-digit Class I recalls. They share the dubious honor of putting consumers last. Moonlight's 11 Class I recalls stand out like a sore thumb.

## A Look Back at May

May 2026 brought a shocking 173 recalls, the highest monthly count since October 2025. Salmonella continues to reign supreme with 152 related incidents this year. One culprit? A batch of milk powder, triggering recalls across diverse brands including PS Seasoning & Spices and Ghirardelli. When ingredients go bad, the ripple effect is devastating.

## The Accountability Gap

It's worth noting: many of these missteps are preventable. A lack of rigorous supply chain checks or adherence to good manufacturing practices (cGMP) is often to blame. Brands like Wellnov Supplements LLC exemplify this, with numerous recalls linked to poor oversight.

## The Bigger Picture

Year-to-date, the 500 recalls represent a historic high--858 have been logged all-time. At this pace, we might surpass 1,000 by 2027. Is this the new normal, or can we demand better?

Consumer vigilance remains key. But the question lingers: Why does it fall on us to spot the risks when multi-million-dollar companies should have our backs?
